check if a string is palindrome - madam
plain java
----------
public class StringPalindrome {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        String str = "madam";

        int left = 0;
        int right = str.length() - 1;

        boolean isPalindrome = true;

        while (left < right) {

            if (str.charAt(left) != str.charAt(right)) {

                isPalindrome = false;
                break;
            }

            left++;
            right--;
        }

        System.out.println(
                isPalindrome ? "Palindrome" : "Not Palindrome"
        );
    }
}

java 8
-----
String str = "madam";

boolean result = IntStream.range(0, str.length() / 2)
        .allMatch(i ->
                str.charAt(i) == str.charAt(str.length() - 1 - i)
        );

System.out.println(result ? "Palindrome" : "Not Palindrome");



E. Complexity
Solution	Time	Extra space
Two pointers	O(n)	O(1)
Java 8	O(n)	O(1) auxiliary space, excluding stream overhead


Use two pointers in interviews when optimization is important.

It avoids creating a separate reversed string.



Check whether a number is a palindrome
--------------------------------------

java 
public class NumberPalindrome {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int num = 121;

        int original = num;
        int reverse = 0;

        while (num > 0) {

            int digit = num % 10;

            reverse = reverse * 10 + digit;

            num = num / 10;
        }

        if (original == reverse) {
            System.out.println("Palindrome");
        } else {
            System.out.println("Not Palindrome");
        }
    }
}

